//# #2745: a projection whose RECEIVER is written at the site.
//
// Codex, P1 round 14 on #2761. Measured on `934b86e`: `"\{(a, 1).0}"` printed a
// 3-digit pointer decimal.
//
// The projection arm answered from a NAME's recorded elements and fell to the
// leaf for everything else, so a literal receiver -- the case that needs no
// record at all -- was the one it could not do. The projected element IS a
// sub-expression of the receiver, and classifying sub-expressions is what this
// walk does; the named route exists only because a name's elements were
// written somewhere else.
//
// Round 13 closed the same arm for a NAMED FIELD and I did not look at the
// receiver while I was there. That is the recurring shape of this pass: each
// arm is correct for the case that prompted it.

struct Qt {
  w: Int
}

fn outer[T](x: T) -> String {
  let inner = [T](a: T) -> String {
    "\{(a, 1).0}"
  }
  inner(Qt::{ w: 5 })
}

export fn _start() -> Int {
  String::length(outer(7))
}
